{
  "version": 1,
  "capacity": 61,
  "_comment": [
    "The region registry — the single source of truth for what each bit of the",
    "allowlist mask means.",
    "",
    "APPEND-ONLY. Never reorder, never delete, never repurpose a bit.",
    "",
    "A region's bit index is baked into every credential ever issued, because",
    "regionCode is one of the three preimages of the commitment the issuer",
    "registered on-chain. Reordering this array would silently re-label every",
    "credential in existence — bit 34 meaning France on Monday and Germany on",
    "Tuesday — which is a total soundness failure that no amount of testing",
    "downstream would catch. tests/parity.test.js pins the sha256 of this file",
    "for exactly that reason.",
    "",
    "Bit 0 is a deliberately invalid sentinel. VeritasCore rejects any policy",
    "that sets it, so a credential whose regionCode defaulted to 0 (a missing",
    "JSON field, a zeroed struct) can never prove anything.",
    "",
    "Capacity is 61: the packed public signal has 253 usable bits, of which 192",
    "are already spoken for by subject(160) + currentYear(16) + threshold(16).",
    "See docs/gas-report.md for why a 62nd region would cost ~6,800 gas.",
    "",
    "`iso` is ISO 3166-1 numeric, recorded as metadata so the mapping to the",
    "real world is unambiguous. The circuit only ever sees the bit index."
  ],
